WEBVTT

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.020
Yeah.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.770
Here!

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.030
Thanks!

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.280
Good afternoon!

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:51.620
Welcome!

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.070
They're nice today!

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.810
Clear, clear!

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.060
To me! To me!

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.940
Keep fighting!

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:27.940
Pass! Pass!

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.570
Clear!

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.700
Number 7 incoming!

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.560
19 to 6, Tsurugaoka Girls' victory!

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.010
And with that, bow!

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.310
Thank you for playing!

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:01.810
Kaede.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.560
Yuu.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.060
Next year you'll be captain, right?

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.320
I'm looking forward to the newcomers' match.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.280
Well then. Take care, Nagisa.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.870
Uh yeah! See you!

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.210
Want a honey-pickled lemon slice?

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.340
They're cold and delicious!

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.800
Wow! Thanks, Shizuku-chan!

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.230
Oooh sour!

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.150
But delicious! Shizuki-chan, you're a genius!

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:49.150
But you just let it soak in sugar and honey.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.530
Eh!? Is that really all?

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.780
{signs}

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.770
Tsurugaoka Girl's Academy Lacrosse Club

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.770
Donated by Hamasuka    Construction

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.780
That's the bus Yuu's Grandpa donated.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.250
Senpai! This was good practice
for the tournament, right?

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:03.500
Yeah!

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.500
Well, I'm sorry for not putting up a better fight...

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.010
Tch. Well we are pretty weak.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.390
You guys used to get along in the past, didn't you?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.890
I've never gotten along with her.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.690
Kaede-chan...

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.820
I absolutely don't want to lose against Yuu, but...

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.780
Right now, our club doesn't stand a chance.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.660
Nobody wants to get better.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.870
I get so irritated that I want to scream.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.500
I don't wanna be captain!

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.290
Maybe I should quit.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.510
Shizuku, do you know what you'll do next time?

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:57.180
Yeah, I'm going to try making Chocolate Brownies.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.130
What's that?

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.220
A type of moist chocolate cake.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.390
I'm thinking of mixing in
almonds and walnuts as well.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.520
Oh snap, sounds delicious!

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.600
Aah!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.390
Huh?

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.400
My mom asked me to do something!

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.400
Eh?

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:12.150
Is that so?

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:13.480
I'll go on ahead!

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.280
Sure.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.030
I'm off work in 3 days, wanna go somewhere?

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:21.030
Got it! I'll text you!

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.130
If Kaede-chan wants to say something, she says it.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:39.630
I love how she is always sincere, however...

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.850
Long ago my grandmother taught me this...

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.660
Pain, pain...

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.910
Fly away!

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.720
All words have a spirit living inside them.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.720
Did you know that?

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.600
It's called a Kotodama.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.600
Note: Kotodama - Roughly translated as "Spirit of Language"

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.480
Kotodama?

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:31.980
So when you're making a wish,

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.320
make sure you put voice to your wish.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.610
But if you say bad things about other people...

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:43.200
it will come back and haunt you.
So never voice those words.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:59.590
Me, Shizuku-chan, Yuu-chan and Kaede-chan
used to play together all the time when we were little.

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:04.180
But when we started elementary school...

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:08.220
...distance started to grow between us and Yuu-chan.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:13.810
Yuu-chan was popular enough to be chosen as the class representative.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.480
PTA Chairman Hamasuka Chousuke

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:18.650
Kaede-chan didn't agree with that decision,
and started to see Yuu as an enemy.

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:21.490
Kaede!

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.110
You're in my group, huh.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.280
Let's have a fair and honest match!

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:29.990
I hope she trips.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.300
Nagisa-chan?

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.590
Take your places!

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.760
Ready!

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.270
Yuu! Take first prize!

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:56.060
Do you believe?

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:56.060
anata wa shinjitemasu ka

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:59.940
There is power in words

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:59.940
kotoba ni wa chikara ga aru

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:05.770
That spirits live within them

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:05.770
tamashii ga yadotteru koto

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.360
Kaede! You okay?

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:11.260
Today I couldn't be honest

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:11.260
kyou wa sunao ni narenakatta

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:15.320
Why can't I immediately

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:15.320
doushite sugu ni omotta koto

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.590
Say what comes to mind

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.590
ienakatta no

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:17.440
How mean, Kaede-chan!

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:18.920
What's with her?

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:22.810
Did you pretend not to see?

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:22.810
minai furi shite ita no

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.340
Kaede-chan...

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:27.900
Yes, someone able to say you like something when you like it

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:27.900
sou sukina mono wa suki datte

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.010
Kotodama really exist!

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:32.630
Someone able to say they dislike it

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:32.630
damena koto wa damedayo to ieru

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.010
Bad words will...

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:34.270
...come back and bite you.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:38.770
That's who I want to become, all the time

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:38.770
watashi ni naritai donna toki mo

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:43.620
I don't need any clever lies

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:43.620
jouzuna tatemae wa iranai

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:47.760
Don't look away

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:47.760
sono hitomi wo sora sanaide

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:50.670
I want to tell you but

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:50.670
tsutaetai keredo

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:48.660
AKOUJI

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:58.660
I can't do it with words

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:58.660
kotoba ni wa dekinai mama

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.630
PUBLIC LONGEGIVITY BELL

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:04.070
I tried my best to become the wind

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:04.070
omoikiri kaze ni natte

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:08.190
I ran down the slope

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:08.190
sakamichi wo kake orita no

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:14.050
I have a feeling that something is about to break through

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:14.050
nanika fukkireru kiga shite

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:19.140
When I was young I was simply innocent

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:19.140
chiisai koro wa tada mujakide

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:23.340
I was able to say my thoughts

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:23.340
omotta koto kotoba ni dekita

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:25.070
Always saying bad things!
I hate you, Kaede-chan!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:21.610
PUBLIC LONGEGIVITY BELL

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:26.560
Before I knew it

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:26.560
itsu no manika

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:23.480
PUBLIC LONGEGIVITY BELL

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:27.570
Why would you say such a thing!?

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:30.990
I began to hide it

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:30.990
kakusu you ni nattetanda ne

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:32.370
I want to just speak my thoughts too!

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:35.670
But, someone able to say you like something when you like it

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:35.670
demo sukinamono wa suki datte

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:40.510
Someone able to say they dislike it

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:40.510
damena koto wa damedayo to ieru

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:46.760
That's who I want to become, for everything

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:46.760
watashi ni naritai donna koto mo

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:48.050
PUBLIC LONGEGIVITY BELL

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:51.530
It's not a clever lie

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:51.530
kiyouna uso nanka janakute

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:48.170
PUBLIC LONGEGIVITY BELL

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:55.800
Look straight into my eyes

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:55.800
sono hitomi wo massugu mite

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:58.620
At the real me

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:58.620
hontou no watashi e

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:06.910
At a place where I can be honest

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:06.910
shoujiki nareru basho e

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:18.250
I want to go... Let's go!

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:18.250
ikitainda ikou yo

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.420
Hello, Frog-san.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:25.590
This heat must be tough for you.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.680
I wish it would rain.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:35.680
Oh no!

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:41.460
But I like what I like

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:41.460
sou sukina mono wa suki datte

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:46.390
Not being able to say bad things

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:46.390
damena koto wa damedayo to ii eru

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:52.670
I'll prove it this time

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:52.670
watashi ni naritai donna toki mo

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.610
Kotodama really do exist!

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.530
Oops...

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:57.710
If I can face it head on it'll be great

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:57.710
honki de mukiaeba iinda yo

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:02.370
I didn't bring an umbrella!

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:01.790
If I could melt the thorns in my heart

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:01.790
kokoro no toge wo tokasu no wa

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.660
My soulful sound

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.660
watashi no kotodama

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:13.300
I'll make it reach you

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:13.300
anata no moto e tonde ke

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:15.600
Kimi no Koe wo Todoketai

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:15.600
I Want to Deliver Your Voice

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:38.530
I'm soaking wet!

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:41.290
Eeh, hurry up and stop!

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.210
It never listens to these kind of things...

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:58.510
Aqua... Marine?

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:04.440
You came too, huh?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.620
W-Wait!

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.580
Excuse me?

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.380
Is there anyone here?

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:36.470
A café?

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.270
Records...

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.360
I've seen these in the music room.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.570
Vi-val-di?

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.410
Huh. I've heard this one before.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:04.910
Is there nobody here?

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:28.770
A mic?

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:33.110
Is this for broadcasting?

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.860
What is this doing here?

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.160
Wonder if it works...

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:55.760
Ah! Ah! Mic test!

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.470
Huh? It's not making any sound...

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.260
In that case...

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:11.480
Then you gently drop the needle here, right?

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:14.820
Carefully! Carefully...

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.110
Oh, it's making sound.

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:31.040
As I thought, it's the song Mitsue-san is humming on!

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.640
Radio... Aqua Marine?

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.520
Radio!?

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:53.600
They're using this to broadcast, I guess.

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:59.990
Ah! Ah!

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.160
Hello everyone!

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:09.540
I'm Yukiai Nagisa, second year student at Hinosaka High!

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:12.870
Today's weather is unfortunately rainy.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.170
On the Hinosaka coast,

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:20.210
there are surfers trying their very hardest in the rain.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:24.180
Surfer-san! It's raining!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.680
He's not concerned. I see.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:30.680
Anyway, that's the ocean.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:35.190
Frog-san might be the only one happy right now.

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:40.940
Frog-san says "ribbit ribbit"!
It's nice that he's pretty easygoing.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.950
How is everyone feeling?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.960
Are you having fun?

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:59.460
I'm a little tired.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.880
What's going on you ask?

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.630
Friends, teammates, studying etc...

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.470
Stuff like that.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:17.480
I'm a second year student in the Lacrosse club.

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:21.480
Today was the last day
before the third years retired.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:28.240
Moving forward, we'll have to form
a new Lacrosse team with the first years.

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.410
Kaede-chan was chosen as the new captain.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.000
I think she's cool.

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:36.830
Everyone is counting on her...

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.840
But Kaede-chan is worried.

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:46.760
Do you aim to be a strong team?

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.890
Or do you just want to form a good circle of friends?

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:54.770
Another thing is Hinosaka High
Lacrosse Club's longstanding nemesis...

00:15:54.770 --> 00:16:00.730
...Tsurugaoka Girls, who have Yuu-chan,
who has been Kaede-chan's rival since childhood.

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:07.570
Kaede-chan never wants to lose against Yuu-chan.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:10.070
So she wants a strong team.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.950
But does everyone else want it that way?

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.790
We got along so well in the past as well...

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:28.430
It's clearing up.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:03.460
Everyone, did you know?

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:07.720
All words have a Kotodama living inside them.

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:13.970
Serious words, serious wishes, will one day come true.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.810
That's why I'll say it here.

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:21.060
Kaede-chan and Yuu-chan,
I wish for you two to make up!

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:30.570
And on that note, thanks for listening everyone!

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:37.080
Please e-mail me if you want at nagisa@deeznuts.jp

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.910
I'll be waiting for them!

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:46.300
Just kidding!

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:04.270
So hot...

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:24.600
Mitsue-san, Mitsue-san, Mitsue-san!

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:25.750
That's mom to you.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:27.500
Oh, you're here!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.800
He has the late shift today.

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.050
Nevermind that, did you know!?

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:35.430
There's a coffee shop in the Hinosaka shopping district,

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:38.890
Right now it's closed for business but it's probably...

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.140
Calm down!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:44.900
If you walk from the temple towards the seaside road,
it's on the corner of the road.

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:48.400
Oh I know that place! What was its name?

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:51.150
Oh that one! Uhm...

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:51.900
Aqua Marine!

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.530
That's right, Aqua Marine!

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.660
They used to do radio, right?

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:58.330
You know about them!?

00:18:58.330 --> 00:18:59.580
What of it?

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:02.790
I-I got a mail! From a listener!

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:06.040
I heard yesterdays broadcast.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:10.550
That's my mothers Mini FM Station.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:17.050
Mini FM is a small radio station that
has a maximum reach of 1000 meters.

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:20.310
It's a tiny little radio station.

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:23.270
My mother was a DJ,

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:24.980
broadcasting for Hinosaka Coast just in front of her

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.900
and for the people in the city.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:34.610
But 12 years ago, my mother and grandpa were in a car accident.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.990
That shop has since been closed.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:42.240
That I heard you yesterday...

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.960
...was honestly just a coincidence.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:57.300
I can't listen to my mother's voice anymore...

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.800
...so please stop reminding me of that.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:06.020
If you enter that house again,
I will call the police for trespassing.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.060
A bit harsh, right?

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.770
Because you sneaked inside someone's house.

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:14.990
That's true, I guess...

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.450
But I thought it was abandoned!

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:21.450
You still can't enter without permission!

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.620
Geez, I get it!

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:29.670
Moving on, summer vacation is almost over and there's the career plans right?

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:30.460
What are you going to do?

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:32.170
Eeeh?

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.880
Is there anything you want to do?

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:41.350
Like, what company do you want to work for
or where do you want to study?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:44.010
I don't want to study.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:44.890
Don't be silly!

00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:48.390
I wanna work at sunrise like dad.

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:51.650
I wanna be a morning driver!

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.440
Kotodama again?

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:57.150
It won't work with you, you don't believe in it.

00:20:57.490 --> 00:20:59.110
Yeah, yeah...

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:02.910
God! Make Nagisa better behaved!

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:04.870
Please!

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:13.750
But I wonder where that girl could've listened from...

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.430
Those radio waves don't reach very far, right?

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:23.050
She probably lives close by?

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:30.600
They're called Yazawa-san apparently.

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:38.190
Grandpa said that 12 years ago,
he held a funeral for someone who had a café over there.

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:42.950
After that they seem to have moved,
and he hasn't seen them since.

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:44.370
I see.

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:46.580
Thanks, Taigo.

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:49.460
Why did you want to know?

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:51.120
That's not your business.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:54.840
You're not gonna shout today?

00:21:56.380 --> 00:22:00.340
Sometimes you come by
and scream into the bell.

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:03.970
You know about that!?

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:06.760
But I've no clue what you were talking about.

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.350
If you tell anyone I'll beat you up!

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:20.280
I won't tell anyone...

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:40.670
Someone's been here after all.

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:42.930
Oh, Nagisa-chan!

00:22:43.380 --> 00:22:44.930
What are you doing here?

00:22:45.430 --> 00:22:47.180
Good afternoon, Shou-chan!

00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:50.470
Do you know what happened
to the people who owned this café?

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:51.520
This one?

00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:55.650
Beats me. It's been a long time since it closed.

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:58.440
Although I think that every now and then, someone comes back.

00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:00.030
Really!? Like yesterday?

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.780
Not too sure, why?

00:23:01.990 --> 00:23:03.780
Ah, uhm...

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:07.160
My old man used to come to this place regularly.

00:23:07.320 --> 00:23:09.410
Maybe your dad knows something!

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:13.000
He should be at home right now, pretending he's busy.

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:17.540
Thanks Shou-chan!

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:25.250
Kawabukuro
Electronics

00:23:23.050 --> 00:23:25.260
Yeah I know, I know!

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:27.010
It was unfortunate.

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:30.430
It was a car accident.

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:33.810
It happened at the curve of
Sunrise Road, near Seaside Road.

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:36.810
Did that cafe run a radio station?

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:38.810
I'm surprised you know.

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:42.070
You're right. The daughter, Akane-chan, ran it, but...

00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:47.030
With the owner gone
and Akane-chan getting bedridden...

00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:51.160
Her poor little kid was so young too.

00:23:51.410 --> 00:23:55.160
Bedridden? So she's not dead!?

00:23:55.540 --> 00:23:58.880
I think she's up at the Rehab Center by the middle school.

00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:01.250
I heard she was hospitalized there.

00:24:19.730 --> 00:24:23.480
Go up the stairs and turn right.

00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:25.150
Thank you very much!

00:24:33.910 --> 00:24:33.950
AZAWA AKANE

00:24:50.590 --> 00:24:52.510
Excuse me...?

00:25:04.520 --> 00:25:06.780
Akane-san?

00:25:14.450 --> 00:25:17.040
This is Radio Aqua Marine.

00:25:17.040 --> 00:25:19.540
Broadcasting from the Hinosaka Coast.

00:25:24.750 --> 00:25:26.920
Mom... Can you hear me?

00:25:40.690 --> 00:25:42.940
In order to reach you this year,

00:25:43.270 --> 00:25:45.440
I think I'm going to try radio broadcasting.

00:25:46.270 --> 00:25:48.240
This is from grandpa's collection.

00:25:49.110 --> 00:25:52.450
It's a song I love very much. Please listen to it.

00:26:58.560 --> 00:27:00.060
Excuse me!

00:27:07.060 --> 00:27:08.110
Who are you?

00:27:08.270 --> 00:27:10.860
I'm the trespasser from yesterday!

00:27:10.980 --> 00:27:12.110
Huh?

00:27:12.110 --> 00:27:14.110
Why did you say it like that!?

00:27:14.110 --> 00:27:14.490
Huh?

00:27:14.650 --> 00:27:17.870
The email! Your mom is still alive!

00:27:18.030 --> 00:27:20.370
You just don't know when she's going to wake up!

00:27:20.370 --> 00:27:23.370
Why did you say that you won't
be able to hear her voice again?

00:27:23.830 --> 00:27:26.630
Don't say things like that!

00:27:27.920 --> 00:27:32.050
If you say something like that,
it'll actually end up happening!

00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:39.720
U-uhm...

00:28:00.780 --> 00:28:05.410
So during the summer vacation
I'm staying with my mother.

00:28:05.580 --> 00:28:09.290
Mhm! I see! Mm!

00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:14.340
I happened to hear you by chance
on the radio yesterday.

00:28:14.340 --> 00:28:17.180
Really! So that's how!

00:28:17.180 --> 00:28:19.590
I'm truly sorry.

00:28:19.590 --> 00:28:21.850
I really liked mom's radio.

00:28:22.260 --> 00:28:27.390
Oh! That's true! I see,
you want to listen to it more...

00:28:28.520 --> 00:28:33.110
I heard your voice, and it made me really angry.

00:28:33.110 --> 00:28:36.030
I know! It was my fault!

00:28:36.030 --> 00:28:38.070
I'm really sorry.

00:28:38.530 --> 00:28:39.750
Tell me...

00:28:39.750 --> 00:28:40.620
What? What?

00:28:41.740 --> 00:28:45.120
Did you listen today?
...To my voice?

00:28:45.290 --> 00:28:48.120
Yeah! I heard it! I listened to it.

00:28:48.920 --> 00:28:51.380
Mom... How was she?

00:28:54.090 --> 00:28:57.630
Was there... Any reaction from her?

00:29:03.760 --> 00:29:06.140
Sorry! I didn't notice anything.

00:29:06.980 --> 00:29:09.600
Well, there's been no response for 12 years.

00:29:09.600 --> 00:29:10.600
It's no use.

00:29:10.600 --> 00:29:13.190
D-don't say it's no use!

00:29:13.190 --> 00:29:16.030
Then, let's just do it a lot more!

00:29:16.030 --> 00:29:17.030
Huh?

00:29:17.030 --> 00:29:18.780
Radio, I mean!

00:29:18.780 --> 00:29:22.660
That's right! If you just keep talking,
I'm sure your voice will reach her!

00:29:23.200 --> 00:29:26.910
Let's do it! I'll help you too, okay?

00:29:28.540 --> 00:29:31.040
There's a thing called Kotodama.

00:29:31.040 --> 00:29:31.920
What's that?

00:29:32.210 --> 00:29:34.710
There's a spirit residing inside words,

00:29:34.710 --> 00:29:37.800
if you voice them properly,
your wish will come true!

00:29:37.800 --> 00:29:39.300
You actually believe in that?

00:29:39.300 --> 00:29:40.430
I do!

00:29:40.800 --> 00:29:42.840
Then why haven't I reached her?

00:29:44.430 --> 00:29:47.270
My words... My voice...

00:29:48.060 --> 00:29:52.770
Even though I've kept calling for her since childhood, even in my sleep.

00:29:53.400 --> 00:29:54.770
That's...

00:29:56.780 --> 00:30:02.780
But I saw your Kotodama.
Some pale purple ones.

00:30:05.620 --> 00:30:06.660
Purple?

00:30:07.080 --> 00:30:12.670
Yeah. Just a little further,
and they would have reached your mother.

00:30:14.540 --> 00:30:17.170
You can see them?

00:30:17.500 --> 00:30:21.170
Uh yes... Somehow...

00:30:27.220 --> 00:30:31.060
My name is... Shion.

00:30:31.850 --> 00:30:34.060
Shi as in purple, and on as in sound.

00:30:34.060 --> 00:30:40.740
Huh? What! Hey! That means they were definitely your Kotodama!

00:30:40.740 --> 00:30:43.150
But, I can't, just because of something like that...

00:30:43.820 --> 00:30:46.070
Either way, it's gonna be fine!

00:30:46.070 --> 00:30:49.080
Let's talk to your mother over the radio!

00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:50.620
Okay? 'Kay, 'kay, 'kay?

00:31:00.340 --> 00:31:02.670
This girl's name is Shion-chan.

00:31:03.510 --> 00:31:07.390
A stylish name, as one would expect of a popular radio DJ.

00:31:09.510 --> 00:31:15.060
When we started with radio,
we first tried to create a program guide.

00:31:16.440 --> 00:31:18.270
Time for us two to talk,

00:31:18.270 --> 00:31:20.400
Time for taking turns talking,

00:31:20.400 --> 00:31:22.280
Time for playing music.

00:31:23.240 --> 00:31:29.490
The most important thing is to reach
Shion-chan's mom, Akane-san from the mic.

00:31:30.990 --> 00:31:35.370
Our words will become Kotodama, and reach her someday, for sure.

00:31:36.290 --> 00:31:39.340
Shion-chan may not believe it, though.

00:31:39.340 --> 00:31:41.760
And although there's no proof of it,

00:31:42.380 --> 00:31:45.130
I believe it will.

00:32:04.110 --> 00:32:05.490
G-good afternoon!

00:32:05.900 --> 00:32:08.910
From Hinosaka shopping district on the Hinosaka Coast,

00:32:08.910 --> 00:32:11.990
broadcasting from Café Aqua Marine Studio.

00:32:12.620 --> 00:32:14.660
Nice to meet you everyone.

00:32:14.660 --> 00:32:16.870
My name is Yasawa Shion.

00:32:17.170 --> 00:32:19.630
And I'm Yukiai Nagisa!

00:32:19.790 --> 00:32:23.300
The title of the program we're starting up today is...

00:32:23.510 --> 00:32:26.930
Kotodama Radio!
-Kotoda...

00:32:26.930 --> 00:32:29.800
Eh, wait! Shion-chan put some spirit into it!

00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:35.390
You're too spirited.
Also, this name you came up with...

00:32:35.390 --> 00:32:39.850
And then, at that friend's house,
there used to be a dog called Kotarou.

00:32:39.850 --> 00:32:42.900
His breath smelled really bad!

00:32:42.900 --> 00:32:44.940
Then she said to Taigo, no I mean...

00:32:44.940 --> 00:32:48.490
She said to that friend,
"Why don't you get a little closer?",

00:32:48.490 --> 00:32:52.490
then she actually grabbed him,
and put his arm in Kotarou's mouth!

00:32:52.490 --> 00:32:55.910
Kotarou didn't like that, and bit down hard!

00:32:57.290 --> 00:32:59.920
He still has a scar on his arm.

00:32:59.920 --> 00:33:01.750
That was five years ago.

00:33:01.750 --> 00:33:09.130
So that's why Kaede, I mean K-chan, whenever she
sees that says "Good thing you disinfected that".

00:33:09.510 --> 00:33:12.100
But that's backwards, right?

00:33:15.390 --> 00:33:17.140
Is this boring?

00:33:23.520 --> 00:33:24.520
What's wrong?

00:33:26.110 --> 00:33:28.280
Nothing. This is fun.

00:33:30.360 --> 00:33:32.740
I knew it. I can't do it.

00:33:32.740 --> 00:33:34.530
I don't have anything to talk about!

00:33:35.870 --> 00:33:37.700
Hey, wait!

00:33:38.710 --> 00:33:40.540
No way...

00:33:56.260 --> 00:33:57.810
Shion-chan!

00:34:00.560 --> 00:34:03.730
Sorry. I can't do this.

00:34:03.730 --> 00:34:05.270
Why not?

00:34:05.900 --> 00:34:08.740
I transferred schools a lot,
so I don't have any friends.

00:34:09.320 --> 00:34:12.360
I've always thought that sort of thing was a bother.

00:34:12.360 --> 00:34:13.660
No way...

00:34:14.450 --> 00:34:16.740
I don't have anything to talk about.

00:34:23.920 --> 00:34:26.500
Then let's make some friends! Starting now!

00:34:30.380 --> 00:34:33.090
Welcome! Huh?

00:34:33.590 --> 00:34:35.600
Nagisa...

00:34:40.480 --> 00:34:42.060
Welcome!

00:34:43.190 --> 00:34:45.230
Sorry to disturb you at work!

00:34:45.860 --> 00:34:47.980
I told you not to come when I'm working!

00:34:47.980 --> 00:34:49.320
Sorry, Sorry!

00:34:49.320 --> 00:34:50.650
And who's this?

00:34:50.650 --> 00:34:53.610
Stuff happened and I made
a new friend, Shion-chan!

00:34:53.820 --> 00:34:55.200
Where's she from?

00:34:55.200 --> 00:34:57.620
You're not from around here, right?

00:34:57.870 --> 00:34:59.290
Visiting relatives or something?

00:34:59.290 --> 00:35:04.750
Uhm, you see, we're hosting a radio show.

00:35:04.750 --> 00:35:05.210
Huh!?

00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:08.210
Radio. You understand?

00:35:08.500 --> 00:35:12.220
I understand, but what do you mean you're hosting one?

00:35:12.470 --> 00:35:19.180
Uhm... Shion-chan has a café where there's a machine and a microphone and an antenna...

00:35:19.180 --> 00:35:23.230
It's a Mini FM. The radio waves will only reach around here, in the middle of town.

00:35:23.230 --> 00:35:25.440
Yeah! That's it!

00:35:25.440 --> 00:35:26.230
What?

00:35:35.700 --> 00:35:37.120
Hello...?

00:35:37.120 --> 00:35:38.160
Yo!

00:35:38.160 --> 00:35:39.120
Welcome!

00:35:41.450 --> 00:35:43.500
What is this place?

00:35:44.040 --> 00:35:47.330
This girl's place. It used to be a café.

00:35:47.330 --> 00:35:49.750
Shion-chan, let me introduce you.

00:35:49.750 --> 00:35:52.010
This is my friend Shizuku-chan.

00:35:54.720 --> 00:35:55.800
Come over here.

00:35:56.800 --> 00:35:58.430
There's something awesome here.

00:36:00.390 --> 00:36:01.640
What?

00:36:03.680 --> 00:36:06.390
We're gonna do radio here.

00:36:06.390 --> 00:36:07.650
Radio?

00:36:07.650 --> 00:36:09.230
Well then, let's get started!

00:36:13.780 --> 00:36:15.820
Good afternoon, Mom.

00:36:15.820 --> 00:36:19.200
It's 25th of July, just past 3 PM.

00:36:19.200 --> 00:36:23.490
Today I've brought some friends to Aqua Marine.

00:36:23.490 --> 00:36:25.540
It's Kaede-san and Shizuki-san.

00:36:25.750 --> 00:36:28.630
Today's broadcast will be by 4 people!

00:36:28.630 --> 00:36:30.040
Huh? Eh? EH?

00:36:30.670 --> 00:36:33.840
Nice to meet you, I'm Kaede.

00:36:33.840 --> 00:36:36.340
There's no kanji, only written in hiragana.

00:36:36.340 --> 00:36:38.050
I'm Nagisa's childhood friend.

00:36:38.050 --> 00:36:39.890
Thanks for having me!

00:36:41.010 --> 00:36:42.890
Eh, me?

00:36:44.020 --> 00:36:48.270
H-hello. My name is Shizuku.

00:36:48.270 --> 00:36:52.320
I'm also Nagisa-chans
and Kaede-chans childhood friend.

00:36:52.320 --> 00:36:55.320
The kanji is written like "Drop"! Thanks.

00:36:57.030 --> 00:36:59.610
Akane-san, can you hear us?

00:36:59.610 --> 00:37:03.160
We made friends with Shion-chan.

00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:08.250
Shion-chan is going to get to hear
a lot about us from now on!

00:37:08.920 --> 00:37:13.840
Today I, Nagisa, selected a record from
Aqua Marine's Classics collection.

00:37:13.840 --> 00:37:18.300
A song that my stepmother Mitsua-san likes to hum.

00:37:18.760 --> 00:37:21.090
It's Vivaldi's "Four Seasons - Spring"

00:37:27.180 --> 00:37:33.560
We gathered every afternoon to chat
about our day in front of the microphone.

00:37:35.150 --> 00:37:38.360
Shion-chan was mostly listening, but...

00:37:38.360 --> 00:37:41.280
...bit by bit, she began to speak more.

00:37:54.750 --> 00:37:57.670
Those words, those Kotodama...

00:37:57.670 --> 00:38:01.090
...would surely reach her mother.

00:38:05.010 --> 00:38:07.010
Indigo Mask?

00:38:07.220 --> 00:38:09.810
It's a radio name.

00:38:10.640 --> 00:38:13.770
Greetings. I happened to pick up your radio broadcast

00:38:13.770 --> 00:38:17.070
and decided I had to send you an e-mail.

00:38:17.440 --> 00:38:22.490
Do you even know what kind of media the radio is?

00:38:23.240 --> 00:38:24.570
End of message.

00:38:24.570 --> 00:38:27.410
Radio name Indigo Mask.

00:38:28.080 --> 00:38:29.080
What do we do?

00:38:29.080 --> 00:38:31.830
Just ignore it! That's the best thing to do.

00:38:32.170 --> 00:38:34.580
But they went through all the trouble to send it.

00:38:34.580 --> 00:38:36.590
Even if they sounded angry.

00:38:37.210 --> 00:38:39.340
That might be a bit of a stretch.

00:38:39.630 --> 00:38:43.300
But this means that this person
is also listening, right?

00:38:43.300 --> 00:38:47.390
In any case, it's better to not carelessly
get involved in these situations.

00:38:47.390 --> 00:38:48.600
Ignore it, ignore it!

00:38:53.770 --> 00:38:54.600
You looking for someone?

00:39:25.210 --> 00:39:25.300
Recording

00:39:29.760 --> 00:39:31.810
Hello! Are we in time?

00:39:31.810 --> 00:39:33.100
Yes.

00:39:33.680 --> 00:39:35.020
Where's Nagisa?

00:39:35.020 --> 00:39:37.810
She went to buy something
so we can get started without her.

00:39:39.110 --> 00:39:40.110
I see.

00:39:54.290 --> 00:39:56.080
You're Yukiai Nagisa-san right?

00:39:56.080 --> 00:39:57.420
Yes that's me...

00:39:57.420 --> 00:39:58.670
From the Aqua Marine studio?

00:39:58.670 --> 00:40:00.550
Ah, have you heard us?

00:40:00.550 --> 00:40:02.000
I am sorry, but!

00:40:02.000 --> 00:40:05.260
Do you guys know what radio even means?

00:40:05.260 --> 00:40:06.050
Huh?

00:40:07.760 --> 00:40:11.140
You didn't reply, so I had no choice
but to meet you in person.

00:40:12.970 --> 00:40:15.890
Indigo Mask is now here!

00:40:17.690 --> 00:40:23.650
And that's why the ideal form
is not like this, but like <i>this</i>!

00:40:23.650 --> 00:40:27.150
Almost like a Kendo sword, you get it?

00:40:27.360 --> 00:40:28.660
I get it, I get it!

00:40:28.660 --> 00:40:31.450
You're not just saying that, right?

00:40:31.450 --> 00:40:33.080
Not at all!

00:40:33.080 --> 00:40:34.660
Well, anyway... Huh?

00:40:39.630 --> 00:40:41.790
Yo! Who might you be?

00:40:42.460 --> 00:40:44.300
You're broadcasting right now!

00:40:48.970 --> 00:40:51.800
This is... Nakahara Ayame-san.

00:40:51.800 --> 00:40:54.810
She goes to the same school as us...

00:40:54.970 --> 00:40:58.690
DJ Kaede-san.
I've listened to you several times.

00:40:59.060 --> 00:40:59.770
Really?

00:41:00.190 --> 00:41:04.360
I thought it would be good
to talk about my field of specialty.

00:41:04.360 --> 00:41:08.030
It's fun and could allow listeners
to find out new things.

00:41:08.490 --> 00:41:09.240
Right?

00:41:09.240 --> 00:41:10.410
Yeah it was fun!

00:41:10.410 --> 00:41:13.910
BUT! Radio is not television!

00:41:14.240 --> 00:41:17.750
Expressions such as "Like this" and "this" that cannot be understood by sound,

00:41:17.750 --> 00:41:20.920
that require seeing in person should be avoided!

00:41:21.420 --> 00:41:24.550
Wait, she's Indigo?

00:41:24.800 --> 00:41:25.550
Furthermore.

00:41:25.550 --> 00:41:26.920
Today's Program

00:41:25.550 --> 00:41:26.920
Talk       (Kaede - Shizuku)

00:41:25.550 --> 00:41:26.920
Music

00:41:25.550 --> 00:41:26.920
Talk            (Nagisa - Shion)

00:41:25.800 --> 00:41:27.590
Those are my notes!

00:41:31.590 --> 00:41:34.010
Sweets time

00:41:31.640 --> 00:41:31.720
(Kaede - Shizuku)

00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:34.390
And what do you mean by music here?

00:41:31.970 --> 00:41:32.050
(Kaede - Shizuku)

00:41:34.390 --> 00:41:37.680
That's picked from the collection over there!

00:41:37.680 --> 00:41:39.350
Those are all records, right?

00:41:39.350 --> 00:41:40.440
Correct.

00:41:41.350 --> 00:41:43.480
Seems to be quite the collection...

00:41:43.940 --> 00:41:46.650
However! When broadcasting radio,

00:41:46.650 --> 00:41:50.360
you must pay a licensing fee to the rights owner in order to broadcast existing songs.

00:41:50.570 --> 00:41:52.700
What!? You need to pay?

00:41:52.700 --> 00:41:55.870
It's fine! There's so many records here!

00:41:55.870 --> 00:41:56.990
It's not fine!

00:41:56.990 --> 00:41:59.870
Even though it's small,
it's a proper radio station!

00:41:59.870 --> 00:42:03.250
You must firmly fulfill all legal responsibilities!

00:42:03.790 --> 00:42:04.810
Is that so?

00:42:04.810 --> 00:42:05.920
Dunno.

00:42:05.920 --> 00:42:07.050
Shion-san!

00:42:07.050 --> 00:42:07.510
Yes?

00:42:07.840 --> 00:42:09.840
I know about your circumstances.

00:42:09.840 --> 00:42:15.010
I think your mother also would want a broadcast loved by the locals.

00:42:16.010 --> 00:42:19.980
Wouldn't it be nice to do it right for your good mother?

00:42:19.980 --> 00:42:20.890
Uh yes.

00:42:21.140 --> 00:42:24.520
What is it that every radio program needs?

00:42:24.520 --> 00:42:25.730
Answer, Nagisa-san.

00:42:25.730 --> 00:42:28.570
Eh? I dunno...

00:42:28.570 --> 00:42:29.530
Next!

00:42:29.530 --> 00:42:30.860
Dirty jokes?

00:42:32.360 --> 00:42:34.030
A jingle!

00:42:34.620 --> 00:42:36.370
Jingle?

00:42:47.250 --> 00:42:51.380
Hinosaka Coast Mini FM Station,
Radio Aqua Marine.

00:42:51.840 --> 00:42:52.800
Like that.

00:42:53.880 --> 00:42:55.890
Amazing, so radio like!

00:42:57.600 --> 00:42:59.270
This is Biwakouji Otoha.

00:42:59.970 --> 00:43:02.770
She attends a women's music school
where she plays the piano.

00:43:02.770 --> 00:43:04.600
A musician through and through!

00:43:04.600 --> 00:43:05.770
Nice to meetcha'.

00:43:05.770 --> 00:43:09.280
Otaha-chi's skill for music is on a genius level!

00:43:09.610 --> 00:43:11.900
But what she played just now
sounds kind of like a funeral.

00:43:12.780 --> 00:43:16.870
I think I'd like it a bit more bright and cheerful!

00:43:16.870 --> 00:43:17.870
WHAT!?

00:43:18.700 --> 00:43:19.660
Then...

00:43:27.330 --> 00:43:28.210
Well?

00:43:29.170 --> 00:43:29.920
I like it!

00:43:40.220 --> 00:43:43.140
It's like a moment in the afternoon...

00:43:48.770 --> 00:43:49.820
Excuse me...

00:43:51.730 --> 00:43:53.440
I found this a bit earlier...

00:43:53.690 --> 00:43:54.570
What's this?

00:43:54.570 --> 00:43:56.160
A cassette tape.

00:43:56.160 --> 00:43:57.660
What?

00:43:57.660 --> 00:44:00.910
Sound is recorded on the tape inside.

00:44:01.370 --> 00:44:01.490
RECORDING

00:44:02.080 --> 00:44:04.330
It says... OA Recording.

00:44:04.330 --> 00:44:07.040
"On Air". In other words, it's a broadcast recording.

00:44:04.370 --> 00:44:04.500
RECORDING

00:44:07.040 --> 00:44:08.750
By Shion-chan's mom!?

00:44:22.770 --> 00:44:27.020
We are broadcasting from Hinosaka Town, Hinosaka Shore.

00:44:27.020 --> 00:44:30.400
Radio Aqua Marine. This is DJ Akane.

00:44:32.860 --> 00:44:34.820
Akane-san's voice...

00:44:36.280 --> 00:44:39.660
Today's weather is sunny, the wind is pleasant...

00:44:39.660 --> 00:44:42.160
...and there's not a hint of rain.

00:44:42.410 --> 00:44:47.670
Uokane's shopfront is already displaying
the saury caught this morning.

00:44:47.670 --> 00:44:51.670
Their bodies are still slender, pointy.
Almost like real knives.

00:44:52.130 --> 00:44:54.170
I could feel autumn approaching.

00:44:54.510 --> 00:44:57.680
I also like grilled saury with grated daikon.

00:44:57.680 --> 00:44:59.590
I like to split the fish open with my chopsticks

00:44:59.590 --> 00:45:03.260
and fill the stomach with daikon.
I just love the bitter taste!

00:45:03.260 --> 00:45:05.430
It's the best!

00:45:05.430 --> 00:45:08.190
Come quickly, saury season!

00:45:08.520 --> 00:45:14.230
And with autumn's arrival, I feel like
playing the usual song. Please listen!

00:45:14.960 --> 00:45:23.670
I'm always watching over you

00:45:14.960 --> 00:45:23.670
mimamotteru wa itsu no hi mo

00:45:23.900 --> 00:45:32.300
What kind of dream are you having

00:45:23.900 --> 00:45:32.300
hoshi wa hikari yasashii yoru yo

00:45:31.130 --> 00:45:34.500
This song... I remember it!

00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:41.630
On this quiet, starlit night?

00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:41.630
donna yume wo miru no deshou

00:45:36.010 --> 00:45:37.420
It's Satie, right?

00:45:38.010 --> 00:45:38.880
Eh?

00:45:39.430 --> 00:45:41.430
Oh yeah, that's right!

00:45:41.890 --> 00:45:43.800
It's 'Lullaby'!

00:45:42.140 --> 00:45:47.140
Have a safe and pleasant trip,

00:45:42.140 --> 00:45:47.140
tanoshii tabi e to itterasshai

00:45:45.180 --> 00:45:48.060
My mom used to sing this everyday!

00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:50.500
My sweetheart

00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:50.500
watashi no sweetheart

00:45:51.060 --> 00:46:00.070
Even if you're having a scary nightmare,

00:45:51.060 --> 00:46:00.070
moshimo kowai yume ni unasarete mo

00:46:00.070 --> 00:46:08.450
Nothing can beat someone as headstrong as you

00:46:00.070 --> 00:46:08.450
kokoro tsuyoku anata wa makenai

00:46:08.450 --> 00:46:17.490
But when you're sad and feeling hurt,

00:46:08.450 --> 00:46:17.490
sore demo tsuraku kanashii toki wa

00:46:17.590 --> 00:46:26.700
Just call for me and I'll come embrace you

00:46:17.590 --> 00:46:26.700
watashi wo yonde dakishime ni yuku kara

00:46:26.910 --> 00:46:35.740
I'm always watching over you

00:46:26.910 --> 00:46:35.740
mimamotteru wa itsu no hi mo

00:46:35.920 --> 00:46:40.810
Sleep well toward a wonderful tomorrow,

00:46:35.920 --> 00:46:40.810
sutekina ashita e oyasumi

00:46:41.190 --> 00:46:45.410
My sweetheart

00:46:41.190 --> 00:46:45.410
watashi no sweetheart

00:46:49.660 --> 00:46:52.370
As expected, the power of music is great!

00:46:52.830 --> 00:46:54.500
About that...

00:46:55.380 --> 00:47:01.510
If we make our own song like her, and sing it ourselves
it should be okay to play on the radio right?

00:47:01.760 --> 00:47:02.680
That's it!

00:47:04.130 --> 00:47:06.640
If that's the case, there shouldn't be any problem.

00:47:06.640 --> 00:47:09.970
It could even be the theme song of this radio station!

00:47:09.970 --> 00:47:14.270
We should all sing along
with your mother and broadcast it!

00:47:14.810 --> 00:47:16.480
The songwriting...

00:47:16.480 --> 00:47:18.270
Let me handle it.

00:47:18.730 --> 00:47:20.570
Otoha-chi!

00:47:20.570 --> 00:47:23.990
Wonderful! I love singing!

00:47:23.990 --> 00:47:25.570
I'm good at karaoke!

00:47:25.570 --> 00:47:27.490
M-me singing?

00:47:27.780 --> 00:47:29.120
It's fine.

00:47:29.120 --> 00:47:31.120
I'll put thought into who's performing it.

00:47:32.200 --> 00:47:35.620
Leave everything to Otoha-chi!

00:47:36.330 --> 00:47:41.710
Thus, our busy little August began.

00:47:47.640 --> 00:47:50.390
Hinosaka Shopping District,
Radio Aqua Marine!

00:47:54.760 --> 00:47:55.010
History of the Radio

00:47:54.940 --> 00:47:54.980
Anyone Can Understand! Mini FM

00:47:56.400 --> 00:47:58.770
First, under the guidance of Ayame-chan,

00:47:58.770 --> 00:48:02.070
we studied how to run
a radio show, and broadcasting.

00:48:02.070 --> 00:48:05.320
Ayame-chan's explanations
were a bit difficult though.

00:48:05.320 --> 00:48:07.280
Everyone agreed on one thing.

00:48:05.650 --> 00:48:06.410
POSTER

00:48:06.400 --> 00:48:07.150
ADVERTISING POSTER DESIGN

00:48:08.700 --> 00:48:10.030
And that would be...

00:48:10.990 --> 00:48:13.080
We needed to attract more listeners!

00:48:19.080 --> 00:48:20.590
To quote Ayame-chan,

00:48:20.590 --> 00:48:23.090
a radio show exists because of listeners.

00:48:28.010 --> 00:48:33.720
We had all the shops in the shopping district put up one of our posters.

00:48:50.990 --> 00:48:57.000
In order to attract a wide variety of people,
we need to broadcast things people want to learn about.

00:48:57.830 --> 00:49:03.000
We collected all sorts of data from
all kinds of people from all over the town.

00:49:08.840 --> 00:49:14.180
I was surprised that so many people
remembered Akane-sans broadcasts.

00:49:14.180 --> 00:49:20.560
Akane-sans Radio Aqua Marine was something that
everyone in the shopping district looked forward to.

00:49:24.020 --> 00:49:25.270
Kawabukuro
Electronics

00:49:24.480 --> 00:49:28.030
Especially the old man
in the Kawabukoro Electronics store.

00:49:28.490 --> 00:49:33.620
The old man was the one who gathered
all the equipment for Radio Aqua Marine.

00:49:34.410 --> 00:49:37.500
And he got to meet Shion-chan again.

00:49:37.500 --> 00:49:41.630
He was really pleased that Radio Aqua Marine was starting again.

00:49:43.130 --> 00:49:49.340
The Mini FM station had too small of an output
and couldn't reach the entire shopping district.

00:49:51.800 --> 00:49:54.220
The old man was an amateur radio geek,

00:49:54.220 --> 00:49:58.020
and distributed several relays, called Transmitters,

00:49:58.020 --> 00:50:01.980
to several shops so that our radio waves
could reach the entire shopping district.

00:50:04.270 --> 00:50:07.690
Since the equipment was installed
more than 15 years ago,

00:50:07.690 --> 00:50:10.780
some of it was broken or missing...

00:50:08.400 --> 00:50:09.900
How is it?

00:50:08.400 --> 00:50:09.900
OK

00:50:08.400 --> 00:50:09.900
Will do!

00:50:08.400 --> 00:50:09.900
Adjust a

00:50:08.400 --> 00:50:09.900
bit more!

00:50:08.650 --> 00:50:08.690
Connected

00:50:10.780 --> 00:50:13.490
...but the old man helped us repair and modify each one,

00:50:13.490 --> 00:50:17.240
helping us to connect the relays one by one.

00:50:19.200 --> 00:50:22.370
I enjoyed talking on the radio on a daily basis.

00:50:22.880 --> 00:50:26.170
Shizuku-chan set up a sweets & coffee shop.

00:50:26.170 --> 00:50:29.260
The shop even attracts Shou-chan from time to time.

00:50:29.970 --> 00:50:34.340
I only hope that he's not coming
for the high-school girls.

00:51:04.830 --> 00:51:05.500
Yuu?

00:51:10.800 --> 00:51:11.630
Kaede.

00:51:12.090 --> 00:51:13.630
You need anything?

00:51:13.630 --> 00:51:15.430
N-not really!

00:51:15.430 --> 00:51:17.600
I'm just passing by.

00:51:19.640 --> 00:51:22.140
Instead of sneaking around you should come inside!

00:51:23.140 --> 00:51:26.150
Although you might be too busy
with the prefectual meet.

00:51:27.980 --> 00:51:29.650
That's none of your concern!

00:51:31.400 --> 00:51:35.160
Now if you'd excuse me.
Give my regards to Nagisa and Shizuku.

00:51:37.650 --> 00:51:40.110
Construction Plan Notice

00:51:37.650 --> 00:51:40.110
Hamasuka Construction Co., Ltd.

00:51:41.660 --> 00:51:43.120
Heey!

00:51:43.330 --> 00:51:45.960
Kaede-chan! Did work go well?

00:51:45.960 --> 00:51:48.630
I guess. So what are we doing today?

00:51:48.630 --> 00:51:51.170
Otoha-san finished the song today.

00:51:51.170 --> 00:51:52.130
Really?

00:51:52.130 --> 00:51:56.640
So we're trying it one by one
before we all sing together.

00:51:56.640 --> 00:51:59.390
Really? I thought we would
just go straight in and sing!

00:52:00.760 --> 00:52:04.390
Otoha-chin will not do such amateurish work.

00:52:04.690 --> 00:52:05.890
Yeah, yeah...

00:52:07.690 --> 00:52:10.900
Well then, let's get started.

00:52:14.030 --> 00:52:16.660
I tried...

00:52:17.860 --> 00:52:19.160
You're too tense.

00:52:19.160 --> 00:52:20.780
Oh! Sorry!

00:52:23.910 --> 00:52:29.960
I tried my best many times...

00:52:29.960 --> 00:52:31.550
Nice voice.

00:52:31.800 --> 00:52:33.010
Eh?

00:52:33.840 --> 00:52:35.260
Your voice...

00:52:35.260 --> 00:52:39.260
It's so bright and dazzling.
As if it were the sun.

00:52:39.890 --> 00:52:42.760
Maybe a sunflower will bloom from this sunlight...

00:52:43.020 --> 00:52:45.270
Don't praise her too much now!

00:52:47.020 --> 00:52:49.270
You get that just from my voice?

00:52:53.730 --> 00:52:55.150
The sound of rain.

00:52:55.150 --> 00:52:56.780
The sound of wind.

00:52:56.780 --> 00:52:59.280
The sound of waves, and sunrise.

00:52:59.740 --> 00:53:01.620
Shizuki-chan's footsteps,

00:53:01.620 --> 00:53:04.290
Ayame's voice, Kaede-chan's voice.

00:53:05.200 --> 00:53:08.290
Everyone possesses their own sound from birth.

00:53:08.620 --> 00:53:10.790
Ah! I kind of get it!

00:53:11.000 --> 00:53:15.550
Sound, or maybe words, possess some kind of power...

00:53:19.430 --> 00:53:21.300
Power of words?

00:53:21.300 --> 00:53:26.480
There's a spirit inside words
and sometimes I can see them.

00:53:26.980 --> 00:53:29.230
This story about Kotodama again?

00:53:30.060 --> 00:53:31.560
Kotodama...

00:53:32.770 --> 00:53:34.110
How lovely!

00:53:34.400 --> 00:53:36.190
You believe in it?

00:53:36.190 --> 00:53:39.360
Kaede-chan doesn't believe me at all though...

00:53:39.570 --> 00:53:41.110
Of course not.

00:53:44.740 --> 00:53:49.870
Nagisa might be an angel
born with an important power!

00:53:51.380 --> 00:53:53.380
You starting a radio show...

00:53:53.380 --> 00:53:55.380
...must surely be fate!

00:53:55.380 --> 00:53:56.460
Is that so?

00:53:57.090 --> 00:53:58.880
Maybe it was...

00:53:59.300 --> 00:54:01.840
Well then... Let's sing again!

00:54:01.840 --> 00:54:02.590
Yeah!

00:54:02.590 --> 00:54:04.390
What an amazing person.

00:54:04.600 --> 00:54:07.890
She can capture someone's heart for a moment.

00:54:07.890 --> 00:54:12.100
This must be what it means to be an artist.

00:56:22.190 --> 00:56:23.440
Welcome!

00:56:26.110 --> 00:56:28.160
It's making me laugh now that I remember it!

00:56:28.160 --> 00:56:29.280
Did you see her face?

00:56:29.280 --> 00:56:30.370
I saw, I saw!

00:56:30.370 --> 00:56:31.490
It was really tensed up!

00:56:32.620 --> 00:56:34.040
A table for three?

00:56:34.660 --> 00:56:37.120
She was always way too harsh on everyone,

00:56:37.120 --> 00:56:39.290
just because she's the coach's favorite...

00:56:39.290 --> 00:56:40.290
I know, right!

00:56:40.590 --> 00:56:42.960
There's no way to keep up with her!

00:56:42.960 --> 00:56:44.800
What do you think Yuu will do now?

00:56:46.130 --> 00:56:48.180
Maybe she'll talk to her grandpa again.

00:56:48.180 --> 00:56:50.640
She'll have to resign as captain at this point.

00:56:50.640 --> 00:56:51.810
She should just quit outright!

00:56:59.650 --> 00:57:00.650
See you tomorrow!

00:57:00.650 --> 00:57:00.940
Yeah!

00:57:01.730 --> 00:57:03.230
We'll go on ahead.

00:57:03.610 --> 00:57:04.940
See ya!

00:57:05.740 --> 00:57:06.990
Where's Shion?

00:57:07.360 --> 00:57:08.820
She went to see her mom.

00:57:09.110 --> 00:57:09.950
I see.

00:57:09.950 --> 00:57:11.070
Here you go.

00:57:11.070 --> 00:57:11.700
Thanks.

00:57:12.280 --> 00:57:14.080
For you too, Nagisa-chan.

00:57:14.080 --> 00:57:16.200
Thank you, Shizuku-chan!

00:57:18.080 --> 00:57:20.040
Smells nice.

00:57:21.500 --> 00:57:26.340
I wish these days wouldn't end!

00:57:26.920 --> 00:57:28.630
Can't think like that.

00:57:28.630 --> 00:57:32.180
Not long until summer vacation
is over and the second semester starts.

00:57:32.180 --> 00:57:36.810
Doesn't feel like that right now,
but we should start preparing for exams.

00:57:37.480 --> 00:57:39.100
Exams, huh?

00:57:42.860 --> 00:57:47.190
This is DJ Nagisa of Hinosaka Shopping Districts Radio Aqua Marine!

00:57:47.190 --> 00:57:52.030
Today's guest is Aqua Marine's pâtissier,
Shizuku-chan! Please welcome her!

00:57:52.030 --> 00:57:55.540
Shizuku-chan, do you have
any dreams for the future?

00:57:55.540 --> 00:57:58.000
Eh, what are you saying all of a sudden?

00:58:01.460 --> 00:58:02.460
Well...

00:58:03.250 --> 00:58:09.300
I've always wanted to be a pâtissier
even since I was little.

00:58:09.300 --> 00:58:11.220
You've always liked sweets, after all.

00:58:12.140 --> 00:58:13.220
That's why...

00:58:13.800 --> 00:58:17.470
I'd like to study abroad in France.

00:58:17.470 --> 00:58:19.480
Eeeh! Why!?

00:58:19.730 --> 00:58:23.730
And I even started studying french a while ago.

00:58:23.980 --> 00:58:25.520
Really?

00:58:25.520 --> 00:58:27.690
Hey, what should we do?

00:58:27.690 --> 00:58:31.610
Shizuku looks like an obedient girl,
but keeps to her beliefs.

00:58:32.610 --> 00:58:33.620
I'll support you.

00:58:33.910 --> 00:58:35.160
Thanks.

00:58:35.160 --> 00:58:36.580
No way!

00:58:36.580 --> 00:58:40.000
What is this? The two of you
have come to an understanding?

00:58:40.330 --> 00:58:43.500
I don't know at all!

00:58:43.500 --> 00:58:44.000
Hey.

00:58:46.920 --> 00:58:48.760
Come with me for a sec.

00:58:53.590 --> 00:58:54.840
What?

00:59:00.060 --> 00:59:03.230
About Yuu...

00:59:04.150 --> 00:59:05.230
Yuu-chan?

00:59:06.020 --> 00:59:09.860
A few days ago she came by here.

00:59:09.860 --> 00:59:11.740
Eh? Is that so?

00:59:11.740 --> 00:59:14.360
I wish she would've shown her face.

00:59:14.360 --> 00:59:16.370
Does Shizuku-chan know?

00:59:16.370 --> 00:59:19.200
No, I haven't told her yet.

00:59:22.330 --> 00:59:23.670
What's wrong?

00:59:27.040 --> 00:59:28.590
She...

00:59:28.590 --> 00:59:31.840
Everyone was against her becoming the captain.

00:59:32.760 --> 00:59:35.050
I heard it from a girl from her school.

00:59:35.460 --> 00:59:35.510
Withdrawal Notice

00:59:35.470 --> 00:59:38.640
I heard everyone resigned simultaneously.

00:59:35.510 --> 00:59:35.550
Withdrawal Notice

00:59:40.680 --> 00:59:42.230
That's awful.

00:59:43.060 --> 00:59:46.230
You don't... see that sort of thing
from her often, do you?

00:59:47.190 --> 00:59:48.650
Kaede-chan...

00:59:49.520 --> 00:59:50.860
So...

00:59:50.860 --> 00:59:52.780
After this I'm going to make a gamble.

00:59:52.780 --> 00:59:53.740
A gamble?

01:00:07.460 --> 01:00:10.250
Hinosaka Shopping District,
Radio Aqua Marine.

01:00:10.250 --> 01:00:13.130
Good evening. This is DJ Kaede.

01:00:16.840 --> 01:00:17.840
Yuu.

01:00:18.300 --> 01:00:19.510
Are you listening?

01:00:21.180 --> 01:00:22.270
I heard.

01:00:22.640 --> 01:00:24.020
About you.

01:00:24.430 --> 01:00:27.020
About the club. That things are difficult.

01:00:28.270 --> 01:00:30.820
If you hear this broadcast...

01:00:31.730 --> 01:00:33.230
Come over.

01:00:33.230 --> 01:00:36.910
Both Nagisa and Shizuku are here every day.

01:00:37.360 --> 01:00:41.030
I have a part-time job
so I might not be here though...

01:00:41.950 --> 01:00:44.660
Yuu-chan! Let's all get together again!

01:00:51.540 --> 01:00:52.630
To Yuu.

01:00:53.130 --> 01:00:54.880
This song is for you.

01:00:58.260 --> 01:00:59.930
This song...

01:00:59.930 --> 01:01:01.640
It's a song composed by Otoha.

01:01:02.310 --> 01:01:04.470
Apart from making our jingle,

01:01:04.470 --> 01:01:08.600
she gave us some songs that she made herself,
said we can use them freely.

01:01:09.310 --> 01:01:10.730
I see.

01:01:11.310 --> 01:01:15.440
Those slightly exaggerated words

01:01:16.030 --> 01:01:21.830
That drifted on a mellow sound

01:01:16.650 --> 01:01:17.610
I...

01:01:20.070 --> 01:01:21.570
...sent an e-mail to Yuu.

01:01:22.240 --> 01:01:23.620
It said, "Listen to the show".

01:01:22.240 --> 01:01:29.420
Are, in some way, my reality

01:01:23.870 --> 01:01:25.620
Oh, so that's how.

01:01:26.410 --> 01:01:29.120
I don't know if the radio waves will reach her however...

01:01:30.250 --> 01:01:34.250
I'm not going to be a child,

01:01:30.880 --> 01:01:32.630
You didn't like it Nagisa, did you?

01:01:34.800 --> 01:01:36.630
Me saying bad things about Yuu.

01:01:35.210 --> 01:01:40.720
But I'm not an adult either

01:01:39.300 --> 01:01:41.550
It's okay, because I knew all along.

01:01:41.140 --> 01:01:45.850
During those difficult inbetween days

01:01:43.050 --> 01:01:45.140
Nagisa is too kind of a girl, I guess.

01:01:45.850 --> 01:01:49.850
Yuu is a lady, unlike me.

01:01:46.180 --> 01:01:49.980
I was glad to be alone

01:01:49.850 --> 01:01:53.650
She needs encouragement. I really hate encouragement, personally.

01:01:54.650 --> 01:01:56.900
I'm sure it'll get through, your-

01:01:55.980 --> 01:02:00.950
Because I believed that I was

01:01:57.110 --> 01:02:01.410
...Kotodama? Even I'm finding this persistent at this point.

01:02:02.240 --> 01:02:18.090
The one who understood me the best,

01:02:14.540 --> 01:02:18.130
Shizuki-chan, Kaede-chan and Yuu-chan...

01:02:18.130 --> 01:02:21.050
...all go through life experiencing a variety of emotions.

01:02:21.050 --> 01:02:30.520
I refused to recognize that

01:02:21.050 --> 01:02:24.680
They live each day facing those feelings head on.

01:02:25.470 --> 01:02:27.430
Everyone's so admirable.

01:02:27.430 --> 01:02:29.680
Everyone's so wonderful.

01:02:30.640 --> 01:02:36.690
I wasn't being kind at all

01:02:42.950 --> 01:02:48.080
I want to look for even more

01:02:48.080 --> 01:02:56.420
Different places when I'm with you

01:03:01.930 --> 01:03:06.760
However, I'm scared that I'll have

01:03:07.010 --> 01:03:15.860
Ushinaitakunai jikan fueteyuku

01:03:24.030 --> 01:03:29.120
When you tell my current self

01:03:29.120 --> 01:03:37.460
To open this lock on my heart

01:03:42.920 --> 01:03:47.760
Strangely enough, I'm not afraid

01:03:48.100 --> 01:03:53.890
This moment will surely become

01:03:54.390 --> 01:04:00.940
A pure song for the future

01:04:09.910 --> 01:04:11.740
Mornin'...

01:04:11.740 --> 01:04:13.910
Hey! Do you know what time it is!?

01:04:14.160 --> 01:04:15.710
Whaa...?

01:04:16.870 --> 01:04:18.420
It's still 10...

01:04:18.840 --> 01:04:21.500
Summer vacation will be over next week!

01:04:21.500 --> 01:04:23.170
You can't be sleeping forever!

01:04:23.380 --> 01:04:25.970
Even if you say that...

01:04:25.970 --> 01:04:29.930
There's an aptitude test when the holidays finish.
Do your best!

01:04:30.140 --> 01:04:32.270
Nice follow, Mitsue-san!

01:04:32.270 --> 01:04:35.520
Oh yeah, that's happening! That's great!

01:04:38.650 --> 01:04:41.020
If I'd studied you wouldn't be in a mood...

01:04:41.020 --> 01:04:43.070
That's what parents are like.

01:04:43.740 --> 01:04:45.700
Hey, where's the rice?

01:04:45.700 --> 01:04:47.490
Go get it yourself!

01:04:48.200 --> 01:04:49.240
Stingy...

01:04:55.200 --> 01:04:57.750
You going to the café today too?

01:04:57.750 --> 01:04:59.080
I am.

01:04:59.080 --> 01:05:00.750
It's quite popular! Isn't that great?

01:05:00.960 --> 01:05:02.960
No way! Have you tuned in, dad?

01:05:03.550 --> 01:05:06.300
I can't because I'm on the road so much,

01:05:06.300 --> 01:05:08.470
but Saitou-san from the train station told me he listens.

01:05:08.470 --> 01:05:12.470
Oh no... Better be careful not to say weird things...

01:05:12.470 --> 01:05:13.100
Here.

01:05:13.100 --> 01:05:14.720
Ah thanks!

01:05:15.310 --> 01:05:17.020
Thanks for the food!

01:05:18.810 --> 01:05:20.480
But aren't they...

01:05:20.480 --> 01:05:22.730
...isn't that property going to be reclaimed soon?

01:05:24.730 --> 01:05:27.650
Hamasuka-san's construction
company was going to build

01:05:27.650 --> 01:05:30.240
a convenience store there
together with the adjacent vacant lot.

01:05:30.820 --> 01:05:33.160
It's by the Sunrise Road,

01:05:33.160 --> 01:05:35.620
so there's probably gonna be
a lot of trucks stopping by or something.

01:05:37.660 --> 01:05:39.080
Since when!?

01:05:49.550 --> 01:05:50.640
Shion-chan!

01:06:01.310 --> 01:06:02.230
Nagisa?

01:06:02.230 --> 01:06:03.730
Yuu-chan!

01:06:05.110 --> 01:06:07.240
So Nagisa didn't know.

01:06:07.440 --> 01:06:11.740
That this property is owned
by my grandfather's company.

01:06:11.740 --> 01:06:14.450
Even though the dismantling preparations begin today...

01:06:14.780 --> 01:06:16.580
You didn't tell anyone.

01:06:19.620 --> 01:06:20.870
Shion-chan...

01:06:21.670 --> 01:06:22.750
Is that true?

01:06:25.090 --> 01:06:27.760
Nagisa! What's going on here?

01:06:28.420 --> 01:06:29.550
That's...

01:06:29.550 --> 01:06:30.550
Yuu.

01:06:30.550 --> 01:06:32.260
Yuu-chan.

01:06:34.100 --> 01:06:37.770
I'm sorry. It was decided from the beginning.

01:06:39.600 --> 01:06:41.640
That when summer vacation was over...

01:06:41.640 --> 01:06:46.520
...Mom was going to get transferred to a hospital near my grandma.

01:06:46.730 --> 01:06:50.030
Are you serious? Why didn't you tell us!?

01:06:50.030 --> 01:06:51.700
You guys...

01:06:54.450 --> 01:06:56.660
got way too much into this.
No one asked for that.

01:06:56.660 --> 01:07:00.960
We did all this for you!
Then you just say that!?

01:07:12.680 --> 01:07:19.100
I'll ask grandpa if he can postpone
it until summer vacation is over.

01:07:19.560 --> 01:07:20.600
Nagisa.

01:07:21.180 --> 01:07:25.310
You can continue to do radio until
Shion-san's mother has transferred.

01:07:26.730 --> 01:07:28.770
Shion-san, is that OK?

01:07:30.690 --> 01:07:32.070
So what's it gonna be?

01:07:33.780 --> 01:07:37.070
Don't step over people's feelings, okay?

01:07:37.410 --> 01:07:40.490
We're not asking you!
This is Shion's decision.

01:07:42.000 --> 01:07:43.660
I'm sorry.

01:07:43.660 --> 01:07:46.830
But if I ask grandfather-

01:07:46.830 --> 01:07:49.090
Grandfather this, grandfather that!

01:07:49.380 --> 01:07:54.970
This wouldn't have happened if your
grandfather didn't buy it in the first place!

01:07:54.970 --> 01:07:56.340
Kaede-chan!

01:07:56.720 --> 01:07:58.850
Say that again...

01:07:59.260 --> 01:08:01.270
This is why people hate you!

01:08:10.230 --> 01:08:11.530
Nagisa?

01:08:13.280 --> 01:08:14.530
Why!?

01:08:15.200 --> 01:08:17.160
Why would you say such a thing!?

01:08:17.160 --> 01:08:19.120
Yuu-chan is Yuu-chan!

01:08:19.120 --> 01:08:22.540
I hate you when you're like this, Kaede-chan!

01:08:26.710 --> 01:08:28.880
What's with all the stuff outside?

01:08:28.880 --> 01:08:29.790
What's wrong?

01:08:30.800 --> 01:08:32.170
Grandfather is...

01:08:32.590 --> 01:08:33.840
Yuu-chan...

01:08:35.510 --> 01:08:37.550
Grandfather is not a bad man.

01:08:39.720 --> 01:08:41.600
Grandfather is working hard!

01:08:42.220 --> 01:08:44.390
He tries his best for this town.

01:08:44.560 --> 01:08:47.140
Nobody tends to notice that.

01:08:48.640 --> 01:08:48.680
Withdrawal Notice

01:08:51.360 --> 01:08:53.400
I just came here because I was invited.

01:08:53.820 --> 01:08:55.150
That is all.

01:09:04.700 --> 01:09:06.290
She was invited?

01:09:08.210 --> 01:09:09.670
She...

01:09:09.670 --> 01:09:11.170
The broadcast...

01:09:12.130 --> 01:09:14.920
She... was listening.

01:09:18.760 --> 01:09:19.760
Nagisa-chan!

01:09:45.870 --> 01:09:46.870
Yuu-chan!

01:09:48.540 --> 01:09:49.370
Nagisa.

01:09:50.330 --> 01:09:51.880
I was looking for you.

01:09:52.840 --> 01:09:54.750
Well done finding me here.

01:09:56.550 --> 01:09:59.630
I used up a lot of time searching through town.

01:10:00.800 --> 01:10:02.140
Stupid.

01:10:08.810 --> 01:10:13.020
After all... People aren't looking at me,
they're looking at Grandfather.

01:10:13.310 --> 01:10:15.070
That's not true.

01:10:16.360 --> 01:10:18.280
You wouldn't know, Nagisa.

01:10:18.400 --> 01:10:23.280
Being the granddaughter of Hamasuka Chousuke,
the greatest contributor to this town.

01:10:24.080 --> 01:10:28.290
No matter how hard I try,
I'll only ever been seen as that person.

01:10:31.120 --> 01:10:35.040
Because I've known Kaede for so long,
I feel that it's too late to start anew.

01:10:35.380 --> 01:10:37.510
That's not true.

01:10:37.510 --> 01:10:41.800
I've told you, that I don't want to see you so down.

01:10:42.340 --> 01:10:43.300
You...

01:10:43.760 --> 01:10:46.390
She probably just doesn't want to lose.

01:10:46.390 --> 01:10:49.980
She probably actually likes you, Yuu-chan.

01:10:54.230 --> 01:10:56.440
I like my Grandfather.

01:10:56.860 --> 01:10:57.940
Huh?

01:10:58.150 --> 01:11:01.950
I respect him and I want him to teach me more.

01:11:03.450 --> 01:11:05.990
People say all kind of stuff, but he always says

01:11:05.990 --> 01:11:09.450
"the nail that sticks out gets hammered down"
then just acts like normal.

01:11:10.250 --> 01:11:11.870
I think that's cool.

01:11:12.500 --> 01:11:15.130
I want to be that kind of person.

01:11:15.130 --> 01:11:16.170
I see.

01:11:16.290 --> 01:11:20.170
So that's why I'm not going to lose to this sort of thing.

01:11:20.840 --> 01:11:22.800
I will not lose to Kaede.

01:11:23.220 --> 01:11:25.010
So cool...

01:11:26.050 --> 01:11:28.760
Yuu-chan, that's so cool...

01:11:30.720 --> 01:11:32.520
What's wrong?

01:11:32.520 --> 01:11:34.480
Why are you crying, Nagisa?

01:11:34.940 --> 01:11:38.480
You dummy. I'm the one that wants to cry.

01:11:39.440 --> 01:11:40.650
I'm so...

01:11:41.150 --> 01:11:42.570
Proud of everyone...

01:11:43.860 --> 01:11:45.320
Really...

01:11:46.280 --> 01:11:47.700
Proud...

01:11:52.960 --> 01:11:55.120
You can take this too.

01:11:55.120 --> 01:11:56.500
Much appreciated.

01:11:58.040 --> 01:12:00.750
Yes! I'll be right with you!

01:12:12.680 --> 01:12:14.770
Nagisa

01:12:12.680 --> 01:12:14.770
Now on air!

01:12:28.410 --> 01:12:31.240
Hinosaka Shopping District,
Radio Aqua Marine.

01:12:31.580 --> 01:12:33.870
DJ Nagisa is on the mic.

01:12:34.250 --> 01:12:36.330
Good evening, everyone.

01:12:36.330 --> 01:12:39.130
Good evening, Shion-chan's mom.

01:12:39.130 --> 01:12:42.380
Today we have a really lovely guest with us!

01:12:42.800 --> 01:12:46.220
She's mine, Kaede-chan and
Shizuku-chan's childhood friend!

01:12:46.220 --> 01:12:47.890
It's Hamasuka Yuu-chan!

01:12:48.590 --> 01:12:50.430
G-good evening.

01:12:50.430 --> 01:12:52.640
Nice to meet you all, I'm Yuu.

01:12:52.850 --> 01:12:53.640
Tch!

01:13:13.200 --> 01:13:14.950
Excuse me, gotta use the restroom.

01:13:23.210 --> 01:13:25.260
Yuu-chan is amazing!

01:13:25.260 --> 01:13:28.010
In elementary school she would always win first price!

01:13:28.010 --> 01:13:29.550
Don't tell stories like that!

01:13:29.800 --> 01:13:33.260
You're smart and you get along with everyone.

01:13:33.260 --> 01:13:34.560
I'll go home.

01:13:35.100 --> 01:13:36.560
But listen here!

01:13:36.930 --> 01:13:39.810
Can you score 100 points without studying?

01:13:40.190 --> 01:13:41.810
Do you think just by having fast legs,

01:13:42.190 --> 01:13:45.110
you could become captain of the lacrosse team?

01:13:45.230 --> 01:13:46.570
Nagisa...

01:13:47.110 --> 01:13:51.740
If Yuu-chan says she wants to become number one,
she'll do her best to make it happen.

01:13:52.320 --> 01:13:53.740
It's hard work!

01:13:54.160 --> 01:13:57.200
Kaede-chan, you shouldn't be so hostile.

01:13:57.200 --> 01:14:02.960
Bad words will become bad Kotodama,
and will come back to bite you.

01:14:02.960 --> 01:14:08.010
That's why I don't want to hear
Kaede-chan say such bad words!

01:14:09.510 --> 01:14:10.840
Nagisa...

01:14:11.340 --> 01:14:13.720
That's really exaggerated.

01:14:15.140 --> 01:14:16.970
But you know, Kaede...

01:14:17.770 --> 01:14:21.400
If you happen to be listening,
I'll just say one thing.

01:14:21.810 --> 01:14:23.650
I'll accept your challenge anytime!

01:14:31.820 --> 01:14:34.530
You're being stupidly hot-blooded there...

01:14:34.950 --> 01:14:38.160
That's all we had to broadcast today.

01:14:38.160 --> 01:14:41.080
Hinosaka Shopping District,
Radio Aqua Marine.

01:14:41.080 --> 01:14:43.380
DJ Nagisa signing off.

01:14:47.460 --> 01:14:49.550
Thanks, Nagisa.

01:14:50.840 --> 01:14:53.260
Wonder if Kaede-chan listened?

01:14:59.770 --> 01:15:02.020
Seriously, she really hates to lose.

01:15:01.260 --> 01:15:04.020
Now on Air!

01:15:01.260 --> 01:15:04.020
Tell her!!
I won't ever lose!

01:15:01.270 --> 01:15:01.390
Come on!

01:15:10.240 --> 01:15:11.650
Shion-chan?

01:15:12.240 --> 01:15:13.610
Nagisa.

01:15:13.610 --> 01:15:16.030
The radio game is over from now on.

01:15:17.240 --> 01:15:20.790
It wasn't for long,
but thank you very much.

01:15:21.040 --> 01:15:24.540
Shion-chan, summer vacation isn't over yet!

01:15:24.540 --> 01:15:28.250
Yuu-chan even got her grandfather's permission.

01:15:28.250 --> 01:15:32.800
That's right, Grandfather said that we
could continue until the end of August.

01:15:32.970 --> 01:15:35.800
It's useless. My mom hasn't heard us.

01:15:36.010 --> 01:15:38.600
That's not true! It definitely reached her!

01:15:38.600 --> 01:15:42.350
It will never reach her!
We can do this until the end of time!

01:15:42.350 --> 01:15:44.560
My mom isn't waking up.

01:15:48.400 --> 01:15:50.650
I gave up long ago.

01:15:52.150 --> 01:15:55.030
So please, just leave it alone.

01:15:57.280 --> 01:15:59.200
You're not really thinking that.

01:16:00.370 --> 01:16:04.460
Because your words just now,
I couldn't see any Kotodama!

01:16:05.420 --> 01:16:08.000
You're still talking about that? So childish.

01:16:08.420 --> 01:16:10.340
There is no such thing.

01:16:10.340 --> 01:16:11.590
I saw it!

01:16:12.260 --> 01:16:15.300
Then why does mom never wake up!?

01:16:15.760 --> 01:16:17.550
How do I reach her?

01:16:18.010 --> 01:16:19.220
Tell me!

01:16:20.760 --> 01:16:22.220
That's...

01:16:22.600 --> 01:16:24.020
Just leave already.

01:16:26.100 --> 01:16:27.270
Nagisa!

01:16:31.020 --> 01:16:32.730
A thing like that...

01:16:33.570 --> 01:16:35.740
Couldn't possibly exist....

01:17:11.770 --> 01:17:13.610
Shion-chan, you...

01:17:13.610 --> 01:17:15.940
Idiooooot!

01:18:04.790 --> 01:18:07.000
Discharged
from hospital

01:19:13.560 --> 01:19:15.810
Looks like we're gonna be stuck here for a while.

01:19:29.200 --> 01:19:30.450
Dad!

01:19:30.450 --> 01:19:32.290
The radio! Turn on the radio!

01:19:32.290 --> 01:19:33.870
Huh? Sure...

01:19:34.500 --> 01:19:36.590
<i>Seaside Road, is currently—</i>

01:19:36.590 --> 01:19:37.750
Shion!

01:19:44.320 --> 01:19:46.680
Shion, this is...

01:19:44.320 --> 01:19:46.680
Hinosaka Shopping District, Radio Aqua Marine!

01:19:47.850 --> 01:19:50.350
Today we're on a business trip in the neighborhood,

01:19:50.350 --> 01:19:52.640
broadcasting from the Akouji Temple!

01:19:53.020 --> 01:19:54.650
To everyone listening to the radio,

01:19:55.100 --> 01:19:57.150
Shion-chan, Akane-san...

01:19:57.360 --> 01:19:59.270
Can you hear us?

01:20:00.570 --> 01:20:03.110
Aqua Marine was suddenly gone,

01:20:03.530 --> 01:20:08.030
But we wanted to make
a proper last broadcast!

01:20:08.370 --> 01:20:12.000
And then so many people came out to see us!

01:20:13.410 --> 01:20:15.540
Oi! Can you hear me!?

01:20:15.750 --> 01:20:17.290
I heard the story!

01:20:17.460 --> 01:20:19.000
Shion-chan!

01:20:19.170 --> 01:20:21.300
Akane-san, can you hear us?

01:20:22.550 --> 01:20:23.630
Mom!

01:20:27.300 --> 01:20:33.310
We thought that Aqua Marine was gone
and all our equipment was thrown away...

01:20:33.680 --> 01:20:39.270
But actually, Kawabukoro Electronics
picked up all the equipment!

01:20:41.190 --> 01:20:45.070
They also helped us set up speakers for today,

01:20:45.780 --> 01:20:48.990
and they also connected a new relay!

01:20:50.280 --> 01:20:56.920
The townspeople were worried about what to do when Aqua Marine got demolished.

01:20:58.540 --> 01:21:04.170
Taigo-kun negotiated with the temple monk
for lending us the Akouji premises.

01:21:06.630 --> 01:21:11.680
Kaede-chan and Yuu-chan handed out flyers together.

01:21:13.680 --> 01:21:18.440
Everyone was listening to
the Aqua Marine broadcasts.

01:21:18.440 --> 01:21:19.940
I'm surprised.

01:21:20.520 --> 01:21:26.280
Akane-san, everyone wants
to hear your voice once again!

01:21:33.370 --> 01:21:35.410
Dad, turn around!

01:21:35.410 --> 01:21:36.080
Eh?

01:21:36.500 --> 01:21:39.420
We can't receive the signal from here. Please!

01:21:40.540 --> 01:21:41.710
Please!

01:21:42.590 --> 01:21:44.050
Driver-san?

01:21:44.050 --> 01:21:45.050
Understood.

01:21:57.390 --> 01:21:59.560
Shion-chan, do you remember?

01:22:00.310 --> 01:22:02.560
The song we practiced with everyone

01:22:02.560 --> 01:22:05.940
has never been played on the radio.

01:22:06.360 --> 01:22:09.200
That's why we'll sing it
in front of everyone today!

01:22:09.490 --> 01:22:11.490
Shion-chan, you sing too!

01:22:28.510 --> 01:22:34.510
I tried my best many times

01:22:35.260 --> 01:22:40.230
To sing my wish to you

01:22:40.520 --> 01:22:45.820
In your eyes

01:22:45.820 --> 01:22:52.740
You actually gave up (Somewhere), probably

01:22:52.740 --> 01:22:58.950
Doing it by myself (Everything's fine) is impossible

01:22:58.950 --> 01:23:03.580
Deciding it was impossible, so I became lost

01:23:03.580 --> 01:23:09.920
But it's different, (Hey now), Look around you, (Is that so?)

01:23:09.920 --> 01:23:14.800
We're following behind

01:23:14.800 --> 01:23:21.270
If it's with everyone, we'll definitely reach her

01:23:21.480 --> 01:23:28.020
Tweet your little voice

01:23:28.020 --> 01:23:34.910
Your words, your emotions, become my wings

01:23:34.910 --> 01:23:42.660
In the heart of the one who received it

01:23:42.660 --> 01:23:45.710
A light is gently lit

01:23:45.710 --> 01:23:52.170
So make your voice loud

01:23:52.170 --> 01:23:58.560
Your words, your emotions, make me soar

01:23:58.850 --> 01:24:03.940
Strength is not being alone

01:24:03.940 --> 01:24:13.700
I want to take this in "Wishes come true"

01:24:34.420 --> 01:24:40.600
That place with the fragrant smell of the salty sea breeze

01:24:41.220 --> 01:24:46.520
The memories we gathered there are,

01:24:46.520 --> 01:24:51.820
Regardless of where you go from now,

01:24:51.820 --> 01:24:58.990
My once-in-a-lifetime (Important) treasure, Always

01:24:58.990 --> 01:25:04.910
There are laughs (Sometimes fights) and jokes

01:25:04.910 --> 01:25:09.580
I show you tears (Sorry) and worry you

01:25:09.580 --> 01:25:15.670
(But it's okay) Isn't it? (Bit by bit) That's right

01:25:15.670 --> 01:25:24.430
If we were honest to each other, "I love you"

01:25:25.140 --> 01:25:31.400
I know that now, so I won't be lost anymore

01:25:59.050 --> 01:26:05.350
Our voices become a chorus

01:26:05.640 --> 01:26:12.110
My heart, my wish, become stars

01:26:12.400 --> 01:26:20.280
At the feet of someone who noticed

01:26:20.280 --> 01:26:26.160
Leads the way to the gentle light

01:26:26.160 --> 01:26:32.670
So make your voice loud

01:26:32.670 --> 01:26:39.090
Your words, your emotions, make me soar

01:26:39.420 --> 01:26:44.390
I see that I am not alone

01:26:44.390 --> 01:26:56.070
Now let's make sure "Wishes come true"

01:27:01.820 --> 01:27:03.530
Shion-chan!

01:27:11.870 --> 01:27:14.960
I reached my mom.

01:27:24.970 --> 01:27:27.510
Hey! Stop slacking!

01:27:27.720 --> 01:27:30.520
We're not!

01:27:30.770 --> 01:27:34.020
I heard that Yuu-chan was reinstated as captain.

01:27:34.310 --> 01:27:38.530
Kaede-chan! We've had enough!

01:27:38.530 --> 01:27:41.360
Come on! Faster! Faster!

01:27:43.530 --> 01:27:45.780
Waaaait!

01:27:47.030 --> 01:27:50.540
And now that the summer vacation,
which had felt like a miracle,

01:27:50.540 --> 01:27:53.080
has come to an end and we return
to our normal everyday lives.

01:27:53.960 --> 01:27:59.880
However, the uneventful days
were also irreplaceable.

01:27:56.540 --> 01:27:56.580
Mystery of
the Universe

01:27:59.880 --> 01:28:03.720
I can't say it very well,
but that's what it began to feel like.

01:28:16.900 --> 01:28:22.110
And as for me, who has managed
to find my future goal...

01:28:22.780 --> 01:28:25.570
Right, starting in 4... 3...

01:28:30.080 --> 01:28:32.120
It's 7 PM.

01:28:32.580 --> 01:28:34.910
Good evening. It's cold isn't it?

01:28:34.910 --> 01:28:38.630
Today Tokyo had the first snowfall of the year.

01:28:39.000 --> 01:28:43.920
You can see the fathers huddling inside their coats
as they walk home and their collars turn white.

01:28:43.920 --> 01:28:46.130
I'm also concerned about ice on the roads.

01:28:46.590 --> 01:28:49.640
Be careful where you put your feet!

01:28:50.010 --> 01:28:52.720
Well then, today's first song...

01:28:52.720 --> 01:28:59.150
Even at this time, I'm doing my best
to not lose faith in Kotodama.

01:29:10.030 --> 01:29:13.620
The inside of my chest was dancing

01:29:13.620 --> 01:29:17.420
As you noticed my flourishing feelings

01:29:17.420 --> 01:29:23.840
The voice of my heart is always saying "Let's go!"

01:29:23.840 --> 01:29:27.300
So start smiling

01:29:27.300 --> 01:29:31.010
Show me your sparking teeth

01:29:31.010 --> 01:29:37.480
I'm going to grasp it "We can!"

01:29:37.480 --> 01:29:40.980
So far you couldn't decide

01:29:40.980 --> 01:29:44.780
Now it's full of possibilities

01:29:44.780 --> 01:29:48.150
To do anything

01:29:48.150 --> 01:29:52.080
To overcome

01:29:49.930 --> 01:29:51.470
A new world

01:29:52.080 --> 01:29:55.160
Let's find the way together!

01:29:55.160 --> 01:30:02.000
A fragment of a wish born in your hands

01:30:02.000 --> 01:30:08.840
Hold up your words to the bright blue sky

01:30:08.840 --> 01:30:15.310
You can't make it big alone

01:30:15.310 --> 01:30:20.850
Keep reaching for your dream

01:30:20.850 --> 01:30:24.770
For our future!

01:30:25.320 --> 01:30:28.780
If the dancing hurt

01:30:28.780 --> 01:30:32.660
Rest up and talk to eachother

01:30:32.660 --> 01:30:39.000
Always show your courage "Let's try!"

01:30:39.000 --> 01:30:42.460
To say what you can't say

01:30:42.460 --> 01:30:46.250
Stop covering up your feelings

01:30:46.250 --> 01:30:52.640
It's important to say "We love!"

01:30:52.640 --> 01:30:56.140
Starting from here

01:30:56.140 --> 01:30:59.890
No matter how much you might regret it

01:30:59.890 --> 01:31:03.350
Today we're going to overcome

01:31:03.350 --> 01:31:06.900
We'll show how to overcome

01:31:05.090 --> 01:31:06.640
I'll be strong

01:31:06.900 --> 01:31:10.280
We'll show you now for sure!

01:31:10.280 --> 01:31:17.200
Grab a fragment of a wish with both hands

01:31:17.200 --> 01:31:24.040
That exact shape is not the same

01:31:24.040 --> 01:31:30.420
You can't reach freedom alone

01:31:30.420 --> 01:31:33.890
My words of love is rushing out

01:31:33.890 --> 01:31:39.970
Stop waiting! For our wonderful future!

01:31:40.390 --> 01:31:43.900
It's not easy,

01:31:43.900 --> 01:31:47.320
But let's to an attempt

01:31:47.320 --> 01:31:53.320
I know how so let's put our strength together

01:31:54.070 --> 01:32:01.580
When you've held this fragment tight

01:32:01.580 --> 01:32:10.840
It'll come out lively from your heart!

01:32:28.730 --> 01:32:35.740
A fragment of a wish born in your hands

01:32:35.740 --> 01:32:42.620
Hold up your words to the bright blue sky

01:32:42.620 --> 01:32:49.040
You can't make it big alone

01:32:49.040 --> 01:32:54.590
Keep reaching for your dream

01:32:54.590 --> 01:32:59.220
For our future!

01:32:59.220 --> 01:33:06.850
From here on... For our wonderful future!
